# Resume pair: seed step.
#
# Plants a deterministic user message into a fresh session and quits.
# The user_message event is persisted to `.zag/sessions/<id>.jsonl`
# synchronously when Enter is pressed (Session.zig writes per-event),
# so we don't need to wait for the model to finish replying. We just
# wait for the user message to render in the conversation buffer
# (proving the persist happened), then /quit cleanly.
#
# Run `resume_last.zsm` immediately after this one (same cwd) to verify
# the seed message renders when zag re-opens via `--last`. The pair is
# best-effort: if any other zag instance writes a session between the
# two runs, `--last` may pick that one up instead.

spawn ./zig-out/bin/zag
wait_text /Welcome to zag/
wait_idle 500ms
send "zag-resume-seed-token-FT4" <Enter>
wait_text /zag-resume-seed-token-FT4/ 5s
send "/quit" <Enter>
wait_exit
